\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{Architecture of a three-layer low-rank random-feature network. The first layer consists of frozen random features, the second layer employs a low-rank mixing matrix $L$ of rank $r\ll N$, and the third layer contains trainable weights $w_2$. The red dashed box highlights the low-rank bottleneck that reduces dimensionality from $N$ to $r$ channels.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
